00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.103
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.103 --> 00:00:04.790
Today's message is expect the unexpected.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.435
Over to you, George Soros.

00:00:06.435 --> 00:00:08.478
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.478 --> 00:00:11.108
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:13.789
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:17.946
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.946 --> 00:00:19.151
- George, you've written,

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:21.701
"The second world war gave me a lesson

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.621
"that I've never forgotten."

00:00:23.621 --> 00:00:24.923
What was the lesson?

00:00:24.923 --> 00:00:28.400
- The main lesson that I learned

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.817
during the war is

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.164
to expect the unexpected

00:00:34.004 --> 00:00:36.671
The situations that you get into

00:00:38.164 --> 00:00:42.646
are so out of context with
what you have grown up with

00:00:42.646 --> 00:00:44.646
that you have to examine

00:00:46.152 --> 00:00:49.227
the framework in which you think

00:00:49.227 --> 00:00:50.916
and then you realize

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:54.249
that we all work with preconceived ideas

00:00:56.356 --> 00:01:00.460
and those ideas don't necessarily
correspond to reality.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.844
So there is this gap between
perception and reality

00:01:03.844 --> 00:01:07.887
and that's the gap that I
have really kind of explored

00:01:07.887 --> 00:01:09.470
and also exploited.

00:01:13.694 --> 00:01:14.548
- [Narrator] After the war,

00:01:14.548 --> 00:01:17.302
Soros left Hungary and went to England

00:01:17.302 --> 00:01:19.656
to the London School of Economics.

00:01:19.656 --> 00:01:21.471
- So I think we all grew
up with a set of beliefs

00:01:21.471 --> 00:01:22.616
that came from our parents,

00:01:22.616 --> 00:01:24.527
our family, our friends, our surroundings

00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:26.197
and a lot of those help us

00:01:26.197 --> 00:01:28.124
but a lot of them limit us as well.

00:01:28.124 --> 00:01:30.452
And so unless you want to live a life

00:01:30.452 --> 00:01:33.527
that's exactly like the people around you

00:01:33.527 --> 00:01:35.556
then you need to start to question things,

00:01:35.556 --> 00:01:37.948
question some of the beliefs
that you grew up with

00:01:37.948 --> 00:01:40.374
and understand are these
actually representative

00:01:40.374 --> 00:01:42.220
of what you're about or not.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.701
This is why actually finding the one word

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:44.821
is really important,

00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:46.079
having the self-awareness to know

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:47.335
what it is that you stand for,

00:01:47.335 --> 00:01:49.552
what the most important
thing is in your life

00:01:49.552 --> 00:01:51.363
and then building around that,

00:01:51.363 --> 00:01:52.982
both a business and a life

00:01:52.982 --> 00:01:54.399
that now has purpose and meaning

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:56.231
instead of accidentally having things

00:01:56.231 --> 00:01:58.318
randomly happening to you that help you.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.151
Now we're setting out

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:01.351
to create a more powerful course forward,

00:02:01.351 --> 00:02:03.664
having that self-awareness really helps.

00:02:03.664 --> 00:02:05.338
Let's look at your beliefs around money.

00:02:05.338 --> 00:02:06.171
I don't think many people

00:02:06.171 --> 00:02:08.863
grew up with a healthy
belief around money.

00:02:08.863 --> 00:02:11.031
Some people believe money is everything,

00:02:11.031 --> 00:02:12.685
all that matters is money

00:02:12.685 --> 00:02:15.007
and some people believe that
money is the root of all evil.

00:02:15.007 --> 00:02:15.840
Right?

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.085
Money is negative

00:02:17.085 --> 00:02:18.264
and you shouldn't do it.

00:02:18.264 --> 00:02:20.628
And anybody who goes for money is greedy.

00:02:20.628 --> 00:02:24.022
If you grew up believing
that money is evil

00:02:24.022 --> 00:02:25.244
and it's greedy to ask for money

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.252
then you never charge what you're worth.

00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:28.418
If you're an entrepreneur,

00:02:28.418 --> 00:02:30.469
one of the things that we
are terrible at in general

00:02:30.469 --> 00:02:31.603
is charging what we're worth.

00:02:31.603 --> 00:02:34.180
Most entrepreneurs should
be increasing their prices

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:35.657
by at least 30%

00:02:35.657 --> 00:02:37.993
based on the value they're
actually providing.

00:02:37.993 --> 00:02:39.587
We undersell ourselves

00:02:39.587 --> 00:02:41.944
and often that comes from
a belief around money.

00:02:41.944 --> 00:02:42.777
Or if you want to go

00:02:42.777 --> 00:02:44.582
and have the impact that you want to have,

00:02:44.582 --> 00:02:45.815
you want to be able to build a team,

00:02:45.815 --> 00:02:47.350
you want to be able to
help your community.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.961
You want to give back to causes,

00:02:48.961 --> 00:02:50.852
you want to build a real business

00:02:50.852 --> 00:02:52.655
you might have to charge more.

00:02:52.655 --> 00:02:53.488
But you'll never do it

00:02:53.488 --> 00:02:55.210
until you fix your belief around money.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.396
And so understanding
what your beliefs are,

00:02:58.396 --> 00:03:01.629
understanding the person
that you actually want to be,

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:03.651
understanding what your one word is

00:03:03.651 --> 00:03:07.276
and then seeing the limiting
beliefs that you have

00:03:07.276 --> 00:03:08.904
and the positive ones that you want to use

00:03:08.904 --> 00:03:10.855
to reinforce and build yourself up

00:03:10.855 --> 00:03:12.665
make a huge difference.

00:03:12.665 --> 00:03:15.923
This is your blueprint and
until you recognize it,

00:03:15.923 --> 00:03:17.396
until you audit it,

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.007
until you examine it,

00:03:19.007 --> 00:03:20.769
you're going to continue
running the same patterns

00:03:20.769 --> 00:03:22.842
over and over and over
and over and over again.

00:03:22.842 --> 00:03:25.053
No matter what strategy
somebody gives you,

00:03:25.053 --> 00:03:26.657
you're never going to
really follow through on it

00:03:26.657 --> 00:03:29.347
because the blueprint that you're running

00:03:29.347 --> 00:03:30.903
is holding you back.

00:03:30.903 --> 00:03:32.412
That's why for a lot of these things,

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.060
the strategy itself doesn't really matter,

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.233
like how to go out and do
this doesn't really matter

00:03:38.233 --> 00:03:39.815
because if you're not ready for it,

00:03:39.815 --> 00:03:42.216
if you're still holding yourself
back with the same story

00:03:42.216 --> 00:03:44.344
that you've been telling
yourself your whole life,

00:03:44.344 --> 00:03:45.745
those sets of limiting beliefs

00:03:45.745 --> 00:03:46.968
will continue to hold you back

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:47.923
until you break through them

00:03:47.923 --> 00:03:48.910
and then you'll be ready

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.109
to hear the strategy and
tactics to move forward.

00:03:52.109 --> 00:03:53.249
So the question of the day today is,

00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:55.898
I'm curious, what's the
biggest limiting belief

00:03:55.898 --> 00:03:58.889
that you have, that you have recognized

00:03:58.889 --> 00:04:00.260
and are trying to break through

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.098
or have recently broken through on?

00:04:02.098 --> 00:04:03.572
Leave it down the comments below.

00:04:03.572 --> 00:04:05.006
I'm super curious to find out.

